{
  "id": "29504_guuhatsu",
  "headword": "{偶発|ぐうはつ}",
  "reading": "ぐうはつ",
  "romaji": "guuhatsu",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "accidental occurrence; happening by chance",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "accidental occurrence; happening by chance",
      "explanation": "Something occurring unexpectedly and by chance, rather than by plan or necessity. Often used of accidents, incidents, and unforeseen events."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29504_guuhatsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{事故|じこ}が{偶発|ぐうはつ}する。",
      "english": "An accident happens by chance.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29504_guuhatsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "それは{偶発|ぐうはつ}{的|てき}な{出来事|できごと}に{過|す}ぎない。",
      "english": "That is nothing more than a chance event.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29504_guuhatsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{戦争|せんそう}は、{小|ちい}さな{偶発|ぐうはつ}{的|てき}な{衝突|しょうとつ}から{始|はじ}まることもある。",
      "english": "War can sometimes begin from a small, accidental clash.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Combines {偶|ぐう} (by chance) + {発|はつ} (occur, emit). An unplanned, chance occurrence. Very often used in the na-adjective form {偶発|ぐうはつ}{的|てき} (accidental, fortuitous).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {偶発|ぐうはつ}{的|てき}: accidental; by chance\n- {偶発|ぐうはつ}{事故|じこ}: a chance accident\n- {偶発|ぐうはつ}{的|てき}な{事件|じけん}: an accidental incident\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {突発|とっぱつ}: sudden outbreak — emphasizes suddenness rather than chance\n- {必然|ひつぜん}: inevitability — the opposite, something bound to happen",
